# Sep-2026 auto-commit sweep hardening — files getting swept in by the platform
# auto-commit hook that must never be tracked. Rules for __pycache__/ and
# .ruff_cache/ already exist above but were added after files were staged; the
# git rm --cached pass in this same commit removes the tracked copies so the
# rules can actually bite.
backend/logs/integrity_dump_*.json
frontend/node_modules/.vite/

frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/48.pack
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/64.pack

# Feb-2026 — Prevent the platform auto-commit hook from sweeping
# in-flight phase specs and follow-up notes into random commits.
# Existing already-tracked files (per ``git ls-files memory/``)
# stay tracked; this rule only affects future untracked additions
# under the ``SPEC_`` / ``FOLLOWUP_`` prefixes. Everything else in
# ``memory/`` (``PRD.md``, ``auth_testing.md``, diag / audit /
# feature / runbook / diagnostic docs) remains freely trackable.
memory/SPEC_*.md
memory/FOLLOWUP_*.md

# CLEAN-1 · Feb-2026 — these build caches are per-dev-machine
# artifacts. Never commit them. node_modules/ above is a catchall;
# these two patterns are belt-and-suspenders so a bad grep-pattern
# future edit to the catchall cannot regress the historical mistake
# (9260 .cache files were tracked prior to CLEAN-1).
node_modules/.cache/
node_modules/.vite/

# CLEAN-5 · Feb-2026 — ``yarn build`` emits the webpack production
# bundle into ``frontend/build/`` (asset-manifest.json, index.html,
# static/js/*, static/css/*, plus mirrored copies of /public/).
# These artifacts are per-build, content-hashed, and must never be
# tracked. The pre-existing ``/build`` rule above is anchored to the
# repo root — it does NOT bite nested paths. CLEAN-5 followed the
# CLEAN-1 pattern: this same commit untracks 953 previously-tracked
# files under ``frontend/build/`` via ``git rm -r --cached`` so the
# ignore rule can actually take effect.
frontend/build/
